--- a/TODO.md
+++ b/TODO.md
@@ -24,3 +24,18 @@
 - [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:326`: `NewHandler` takes six parameters, with two adjacent `time.Duration`s. Use an options struct.
 - [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go` and `desktop_test.go`: about 25 doc comments open with their declaration's own name. The test file's `contains`/`stringContains` reimplement `strings.Contains`.
 - [ ] Notification bodies are sent as markup without checking the server's `body-markup` capability. A server without it shows `&lt;` literally.
+
+## Unsmell run 2026-11-01 (second pass): typed notification bodies
+
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:itemsSubject` and `internal/cli/format.go:requestSummary` both derive what a request is about (one label, or "%d items"). `slow_upstream.go` spells "(%d items)" a third time. They have already diverged: an empty search shows "all" on the desktop and "-" in the CLI. Move one method onto `approval.Request` and decide which empty-search text wins.
+- [ ] `commitSubject` (first line of a commit message) is written in `internal/notification/desktop.go`, `internal/cli/format.go:212` and inline in `internal/api/gpgsign.go:95`. Make it a method on `approval.GPGSignInfo`.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream.go:itemDisplayLabel` falls back to the item's Path when it has no Label, but `desktop.go` (`sshSubject`, `itemsSubject`) uses `Label` raw, so a path-only item shows an empty label there. Move the rule onto `approval.ItemInfo` and use it in both bodies. This changes what desktop notifications show.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go`: per-request-type rules live in three `switch req.Type` blocks (`notificationMeta`, `formatBody`, `itemsSubject`). Gather them into one per-type table or into methods on `approval.RequestType`. `notificationMeta` also never uses its receiver.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go`: `notifications` and `requests` form a bidirectional map that is kept in sync by hand in five places (`forget`/remember pairs in `sendNotification`, `handleCancelled`, `handleResolved`, the action handler). Extract a small two-way map type. `notifier.Close` plus its "failed to close notification" log is also written twice.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:handleCancelled` does four jobs: cancel, close, store and prune, then build and send the follow-up. Split it into named steps.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:doNotifyFull`: `expireTimeout` uses sentinel ints (-1 is the server default, 0 is never) and urgency is a bare byte. Use typed constants. `(summary, body, icon, actions)` travels together through four functions; consider a notification struct. The trailing `// summary`, `// body` comments on the D-Bus call restate the arguments.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:380` builds `"?request="` by concatenation, and `web/src/App.svelte:173` reads `params.get("request")`. Build the URL with `net/url` from one named parameter.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go`: `"ActionInvoked"` is spelled three times (desktop.go:88, :140, desktop_test.go:1020), and the channel buffer size 16 appears five times. The reconnect doc (desktop.go:99) narrates its steps, and the trailing comment at desktop.go:304 joins two ideas with a semicolon. Request IDs (string) and notification IDs (uint32) are bare types.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream.go`: `NewSlowUpstreamNotifier` and `newSlowUpstreamNotifier` have identical bodies, and the second's doc names its caller ("for testing"). Keep one. All seven docs in the file open with their declaration's own name. `NotifySlowUpstream`'s doc narrates ("then returns") and does not say the dismiss function is a no-op when the send failed. The icon `"dialog-password"` is spelled here and three times in `desktop.go:notificationMeta`.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream_test.go`: the mock and notifier setup and the locked `mock.notified[0]` read are repeated in about 12 tests. Several index `[0]` without a length check, so a failure panics. Use `mockNotifier.lastNotify`, and make the four summary tests one table.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop_test.go`: `newTestHandler` duplicates `newTestHandlerWithDelay`. The ListenActions goroutine, sleep and cancel block is repeated five times, and the notification-ID lookup under the lock four times. The GetSecret fixture is built inline about ten times. The connect helper at :1018 duplicates `DBusNotifier.connect`. `notifID := …; _ = notifID` and `_ = mock` are dead code. `mockApprover` encodes the call kind as an "auto:"/"approve_auto:" string prefix.
